          %p
          %h2#section_Idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of a
            %em sketch
            (
            %a{:href => "#BastianiEhresmann72"}> Bastiani &amp; Ehresmann 1972
            ) is one formalisation of the notion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagrammatic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            of the theory (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"}> finite products
            , say). On the other hand, it is not a very concise notion: as Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExampleSketchUnitalMagmas"}
            illustrates, writing down the full details of a sketch even in the simplest examples takes time!
          %p
            There is a precise correspondence between categories of models of sketches and
            = succeed "\u00A0and" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable categories
          %p
            The notion of a sketch generalises that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExampleLawvereTheory"}
          %p
          %h2#section_Details Details
          %p
          %h3#section_Sketches Sketches
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em sketch
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              equipped with a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              and a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocones"} cocones
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
              equipped with a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagrams
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocones"} cocones
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em realized sketch
              is one where all the cones in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              cones and all the cocones in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              cocones.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em limit sketch
              is a sketch with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \emptyset
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em colimit sketch
              is a sketch with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L = \emptyset
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em finite product sketch
              is a limit sketch in which the only cones are those of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+product"} finite product
              diagrams.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em finite limit sketch
              is a limit sketch in which the only cones are those of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              diagrams.
          %p
          %h3#section_Models_of_sketches Models of sketches
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em model of a sketch
              in a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\to \mathcal{C}
              taking each cone in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              to a limit cone and each cocone in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              to a colimit cocone.
          %p
            In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is realized if and only if its identity functor is a model.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              If one takes the definition of a sketch to be that involving directed graphs, a
              %em model of a sketch
              in a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a morphism of directed graphs from the directed graph of the sketch to the underlying directed graph of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            Frequently the notion of model is restricted to the case
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}=Set
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              is
              %em sketchable
              if it is the category of models (in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
          %h2#section_Examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p A sketch, more precisely a finite product sketch, for the theory of pointed sets can be constructed as follows. The directed graph can be taken to be the following.
            %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
              %svg{:height => "18.711", :viewbox => "0 0 103.234 18.711", :width => "103.234", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
