            %p
              commute to really be the product of the arrows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{X}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id
            %p
              The arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is sent to a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m: X \times X \rightarrow X
              which is arbitrary except that the diagrams
