          %p
          #ExampleLawvereTheory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              is a special case of a (limit) sketch, where the category is one with a distinguished object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that all objects are (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
              to) powers of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \emptyset
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is the set of all product cones.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToLocallyRepresentableCategories Relation to accessible and locally representable categories
          %p
          #LimitSketchableCategoriesAreAccessible.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The categories of models of sketches are equivalently the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+categories"} accessible categories
          %p
          #LimitSketchableCategoriesAreLocallyPresentable.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The categories of models of limit-sketches are the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
          (
          %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický49"}> Adámek &amp; Rosický 1994, Cor. 1.52
          )
          .num_prop
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p From the discussion there we have that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
                  is equivalently:
                %ul
                  %li
                    a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                    of a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
                    that’s closed under
                    = succeed "-filtered" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi κ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  %li the category of models of a sketch
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
                  is equivalently:
                %ul
                  %li
                    a
                    %em reflective
                    full subcategory of a presheaf category that’s closed under
                    = succeed "-filtered" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi κ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  %li
                    the category of models of a
                    %em limit
                    sketch
                  %li an accessible category with all small limits
                  %li an accessible category with all small colimits
            %p We can “break in half” the difference between the two and define
            %ul
              %li
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+multipresentable+category"} locally multipresentable category
                to be equivalently:
                %ul
                  %li
                    a
                    %em multireflective
                    full subcategory of a presheaf category that’s closed under
                    = succeed "-filtered" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi κ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  %li
                    the category of models of a
                    %em limit and coproduct
                    sketch
                  %li
                    an accessible category with all small
                    %em connected
                    limits
                  %li an accessible category with all small multicolimits
            %p and
            %ul
              %li
                a
                %em weakly locally presentable category
                to be equivalently:
                %ul
                  %li
                    a
                    %em weakly reflective
                    full subcategory of a presheaf category that’s closed under
                    = succeed "-filtered" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi κ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  %li
                    the category of models of a
                    %em limit and epi
                    sketch
                  %li an accessible category with all small products
                  %li an accessible category with all small weak colimits
          %h3#monoidal_structures_on_the_category_of_sketches Monoidal Structures on the Category of Sketches
          %p The category of sketches is well behaved: it is complete, cocomplete, cartesian closed and has a second symmetric monoidal closed structure.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The category of sketches is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+category"} topological
              over the category of directed
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/pseudograph"} pseudographs
          %p The above proposition gives the category of sketches Cartesian products - however these are often not the sketches one would expect when thinking of the product of two theories. Instead consider the tensor product:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S,T
              be sketches. We define the sketch
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \otimes T
              to be:
            %p
              The vertices of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \otimes T
              are the product of the set of vertices from
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Edge
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Vertex
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Vertex
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Edge
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ (\alpha, b) | \alpha \in \mathsf{Edge}(S), b \in \mathsf{Vertex}(T)\}
                    \\cup \{ (a, \beta) | a \in \mathsf{Vertex}(S), \beta \in \mathsf{Edge}(T)\}
            %p
              where the source of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
