            %ul
              %li
                The set of cones and cocones are define analogously to the set of commuting diagrams, except
                %em only
                the vertical and horizontal cones are taken.
            %p
              This tensor product, along with the unit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ast, \emptyset, \emptyset, \emptyset)
          %p This monoidal structure is useful for considering structures like double categories (i.e. categories in the category of categories).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S,T
              be sketches, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              some category. Then the category of models of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              in the category of models of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is equivalent to the category of models of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \otimes T
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            One can ask when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \otimes T
            has the same models as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \otimes S
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-models." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            In general one can not swap the order in the monoidal product. For example take the (terminal object + coproduct)-sketch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            whose models are maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X \coprod 1
            and the finite product sketch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            whose models are monoids. Look at models of these in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-Mod" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-Mod" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Ehresmann68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Esquisses et types de structures algébriques
                %strong 14
                1–2 (1968) 1-14 &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Ehresmann-EsquisseEtTypes.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#BastianiEhresmann72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9e+Bastiani"}> Andrée Bastiani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"} Charles Ehresmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories of sketched structures
                %strong 13
                no 2 (1972) 104-214 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=CTGDC_1972__13_2_104_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1972__13_2_104_0
                )
          %p Overview in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Wells"}> Charles Wells
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sketches: Outline with references
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.217.3531"} citeseer:10.1.1.217.3531
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Wells_Sketches.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on Sketches
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/sketch.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr-NotesOnSketches.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Wells"} Charles Wells
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes%2C+Triples%2C+and+Theories"} Toposes, Triples, and Theories
              %p
                Reprints in
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/12/tr12abs.html"} Theory and Applications of Categories, No. 12 (2005) pp. 1-287
          %p
            and with emphasis on the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+categories"} accessible categories
          %ul
            %li#MakkaiPare
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Makkai"}> Michael Makkai
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"} Robert Paré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Accessible categories: The foundations of categorical model theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-104"} ISBN:978-0-8218-7692-3
            %li{:id => "AdámekRosický49"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locally+presentable+and+accessible+categories"} Locally presentable and accessible categories
          %p
            Proof that not only every sketchable category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible
            but that conversely every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
            is sketchable:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Lair"}> Christian Lair
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégories modelables et catégories esquissables
              %strong 6
              5 (1981) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=DIA_1981__6__A5_0"}> numdam:DIA_1981__6__A5_0
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/DIA_1981__6__A5_0.pdf"} pdf
          %p The tensor product of sketches is investigated here:
          %ul
            %li
              David D. Benson, Multilinearity of sketches,
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1997/n11/n11.pdf"} TAC, vol.11, nr. 3, pp.269-277
          %p
            The category of sketches itself was studied as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            in:
          %ul
            %li#Gray
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+W.+Gray"}> John W. Gray
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Category of Sketches as a Model for Algebraic Semantics
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Brandenburg"}> Martin Brandenburg
              ,
              %em Large limit sketches and topological space objects
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.11115"}> arXiv:2106.11115
              )
          %h3#in_enriched_category_theory In enriched category theory
          %p
            Discussion of sketches the generality of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %ul
            %li#Kelly82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+Max+Kelly"}> G. Max Kelly
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Structures defined by finite limits in the enriched context, I
                %strong 23
                1 (1982) 3-42 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1982__23_1_3_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1982__23_1_3_0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carmen+Quinteriro"} Carmen Quinteriro
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A theory of enriched sketches
                %strong 4
                3 (1998) 47-72 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1998/n3/4-03abs.html"}> tac:4-03
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1998/n3/n3.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#generalisations Generalisations
          %p
            Discussion in the generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            into
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
          %ul
            %li#Street76
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                %em Complete objects relative to a theory
                (1976) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://science.mq.edu.au/~street/Sketch.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Street-CompleteObjects.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#KinoshitaPowerTakeyama99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoshiki+Kinoshita"}> Yoshiki Kinoshita
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Power"} John Power
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sketches
                %strong 143
                1-3 (1999) 275-291 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(98)00114-5"}> doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(98)00114-5
                ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                %em Pointwise extensions and sketches in bicategories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.6427"}> arXiv:1409.6427
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Generalising the approach of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KinoshitaPowerTakeyama99"} Kinoshita, Power &amp; Takeyama 1999
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+weak+factorisation+system"} algebraic weak factorisation system
            is defined in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Bourke"}> John Bourke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"} Richard Garner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic weak factorisation systems II: Categories of weak maps
              %strong 220
              (2016) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1412.6560"}> arXiv:1412.6560
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2015.06.003"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2015.06.003
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+2-category"} enhanced 2-categorical
            limit sketches:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathanael+Arkor"}> Nathanael Arkor
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Bourke"} John Bourke
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Joanna Ko
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Joanna+Ko"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Enhanced 2-categorical structures, two-dimensional limit sketches and the symmetry of internalisation
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.07475"} arXiv:2412.07475
              (2024).
